# The sum of an array of numbers of one limb that the program supplies (milestone2.md, "Arrays that
# the program fills"; question 19, recommended (a)): the sum_1 fold with each element passed
# through guard first (sum_entry_step_1), rule R3. One addition more per element, and the bound
# holds of the values in the array whatever the compiler does. Its claims are those of sum_1.
fold:          sum_1_entry
arrays:        supplied x
state:         s
step:          s = sum_entry_step_1(s, x)
combine:       s = add_1_1(s, s)
orders:        sequential, lanes
writes:        none
output:        r
output:        mask flag
finish:        (r, flag) = fold_finish_1(s)
value:         x
ensures:       fold_error r eps=u/(1+u) rel=n-1
ensures:       finite_or_nan r flag=flag
min_precision: 1
theorem:       proofs/theories/FoldSums.v
status:        proved
domain:        extended
source:        Higham's bound for summation over any tree, with the bound of one rounding
license:       bound: published; proof: MIT
